<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sabvest boosts yr shr, div flat.</title>
<headline>Sabvest boosts yr shr, div flat.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31 1996.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     50.5	  vs     27.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  3.0	  vs     3.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	  26.09	  vs     5.88</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  26.09	  vs    26.09</p>
<p>    Tax			  -	    vs	-</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   7.07	  vs     7.07</p>
<p>Income from operations</p>
<p>    and investments	19.02	  vs    19.02</p>
<p>Div payable around April 18</p>
<p>on register April 4</p>
<p>Full name: Sabvest Limited</p>
<p>    Share of associates' 17.09	  vs    17.09</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said its associates and investments were performing well and prospects were good. It anticipated dividends, headline earnings and net asset value per share of 4-5 cents, 28-33 cents and 350-400 cents respectively for 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
